From c5e4e549c03b2ce098c9d80fb7f0f9ef030c212d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:25:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/32] Reconstruct the virtual environment translation unit

Recover all twenty bodies of osfmk/kern/virtual_env.c from the
xnu-13432 reference kernel: the availability and object-count policy,
the kernel/user argument translation, path copy-in, the refcounted
virtual_env object with its lazily allocated Mach port, the no-senders
callback and its IPC kobject definition, the MIG entry points, and the
subsystem-root-path interface used by the exec paths.

The reconstructed file needs three small deltas in existing headers:
IKOT_VIRTUAL_ENV at the end of the kobject type enum (49), a
p_virtual_env pointer in struct proc, and an osvariant_status
declaration shared with osfmk.  The reference kernel removed
p_subsystem_root_path in favour of p_virtual_env; the old field is
retained for now because the exec and fork paths that use it have not
been reconstructed yet.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
